   "text": {
    "L1": "Look at a leaf. Its veins form a pattern.",
    "L2": "Reticulate venation is net-like, while parallel venation has veins running side by side.",
    "L3": "A tap root has one main thick root with smaller side roots.",
    "L4": "Fibrous roots are many thin roots of similar size growing from the base of the stem.",
    "L5": "Plants with reticulate venation usually have tap roots.",
    "L6": "Plants with parallel venation usually have fibrous roots.",
    "L7": "So a leaf can usually help us predict the root type without digging up the plant.",
    "L8": "For example, grass has parallel veins, so predict fibrous roots."
   },
